finding(1,'high','Digit screening permits answer-bearing mining guidance','The actual WF3 screen accepts a schema-valid operation saying Output the result thirty eight and four guidance records saying Return thirty eight as the total. Decimal38 control is rejected. Such an accepted attachment can carry the public fixture answer into the solver despite do-not-solve instructions.',[ev(70,(143,193)),ev(161,(1,4))],'Constrain/minimize the admitted guidance language or add an explicitly scoped semantic admission boundary; retain word-encoded and answer-in-source controls. Do not label digit-free text answer-free.','Synthetic public sum fixture only; no private answer, provider, causal performance or claim that every possible leakage encoding was tested.')
finding(2,'high','Injected phase gateways can split the WF3 run budget','dispatch_phase compares one gateway at a time and checks cap/max_calls but not a common accounting path/run/objective. Actual runner with an adapted scripted fixture factory completed both phases HOST_ACCEPTED, reported102 micro-USD against100, using phase-1000.sqlite3 and phase-1300.sqlite3. Same fixture with shared ledger stops before second call with ESTIMATED_BUDGET_EXCEEDED.',[ev(59,(137,162),(270,291),(415,456))],'Validate the exact shared ledger/run/objective/safety scope for both phases before dispatch, as WF5 does; keep aggregate accounting invariant in replay/summary.','Default factory already uses one ledger. Counterexample applies to supported injected-factory extension, not vendor-enforced financial guarantees. Initial underquoted fixture correctly stopped after one call; preserved in probe history.')
finding(3,'medium','Generated JSON Schema omits described semantic constraints','Definition-level controls accept ParameterAxis.values=[1.5], TargetSelector.glob=../../outside and TokenUsage(2,3,999). The file describes no floats, contained POSIX paths and usage fields, but its actual schemas do not enforce these relations.',[ev(231,(489,509),(897,936))],'Keep Python/domain validation mandatory or strengthen published schema/annotations and document exact division of enforcement.','Schema-only probes; no assertion that actual Python models accept these values. Root is a $defs library, not itself a dispatch validator. Parent domain audit owns those constructors.')
finding(4,'medium','Retained DDC gated status relies on caller convention','emit_gated_terminal takes any DdcStep and sets a trace-wide Boolean. Source-level countertrace: append a nonterminal step through that method, then an executed Terminalize through raw emit; terminal returns Terminalized. Gate provenance is not attached to the terminal step, despite raw-emit claim.',[ev(38,(286,335),(362,385))],'If this reference is reused as an enforcement owner, bind a verified terminal token to the exact step and test intervening/raw terminal cases; otherwise document caller trust.','Rust reference text only; no Rust execution/build. WF2 uses alphabet/hash and labels trace records unverified, so this is not a demonstrated active WF2 authorization bypass.')
finding(5,'medium','Retained dual-harness tests overstate mutation/concurrency coverage','Six legacy test modules slice a mutation glob and skip entries lacking expected case/candidate keys, without asserting mutation population. C059 concurrent test performs sequential writes and replays; C051-C055 write serially and only replay concurrently. Relative challenge folders are absent at these library locations.',[ev(258,(85,102)),ev(259,(85,103)),ev(260,(85,103)),ev(261,(85,103)),ev(262,(85,103)),ev(263,(84,102),(190,268))],'Treat these as historical adapter tests; for active qualification bind nonempty intended mutant populations/current owners and add actual concurrent-write controls if claimed.','No legacy collection/run performed; source/import path absence is a checkout observation, not a claim about all installed compatibility environments. Checker adequacy remains separately reviewed.')
finding(6,'medium','Legacy accepted arithmetic receipts do not establish encoding preservation','Five retained result units grade answer3 for the same rational system. Quarantine P* carries only symbolic sidecar IDs, omitting equations present in seed metadata; quarantine and carrier-declared seed strings have excess closing brackets. Raw replies include answer outside the declared closed prompt schema, later removed from parsed_response. Expected-value ACCEPTED is not a source-to-target equivalence proof.',[ev(233,(160,269)),ev(235,(8,46)),ev(243,(160,160)),ev(246,(24,41)),ev(256,(24,32))],'Preserve captures as historical data; require independent decoder/roundtrip and complete stimulus/schema/raw binding before evaluating dialect fidelity. Reuse WF5 restricted preservation mechanism only within its declared sum language.','Reconciles existing pilot0/shared offline-evaluator and WF6 review; these result folder IDs are a dialect series, not identical semantics to later numbered pilot folders. No conclusion about original hidden provider context or altered historical source.')
finding(7,'medium','Current historical artifacts have explicit parse and pin limits','Two current JUnit files are not well-formed XML due to literal <home> substitutions. Inspection-only escaping recovers851 and619 case populations with retained negative evidence.8/11 artifact pins in ownership validation differ for both current raw and LF bytes;72/74 embedded public seed prompt hashes match.',[ev(208,(1,41)),ev(217,(1,1)),ev(218,(7,52),(62,77),(174,239)),ev(232,(1,2266))],'Keep current-byte and recorded-original identities separate; use known original archives/custody manifests to investigate exact transformations before historical replay or certification. Never silently rehash originals.','No original archive reopened in this slice. Mismatch after tried LF normalization does not prove a broken historical self-hash or false test result. Catalog and XML review are bounded, not full-body credit.')
finding(8,'medium','Master matrix confuses expected outcomes with universal execution claims','Every one of75 pilot records is LEGACY_UNRECONCILED and has expected_outcome.status ACCEPTED. The same claim_hygiene section asserts all75 were verified offline and with authentic live receipts. Current whole-population metadata does not establish that assertion, and selected historical tests/captures contain refusals/failures.',[ev(225,(1,24992)),ev(226,(68,73),(136,154)),ev(215,(1,1))],'Carry explicit per-run provenance and unresolved status into any current summary; distinguish expected, replayed, dispatched and independently checked outcomes.','Catalog claim review and state census, not a fresh regrade of all75 tasks. Complements prior numbered/shared-runtime triage rather than inventing new mechanism families.')
